From b2874e8ef5005ce09b53e0f6cd525f5904fe7e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:19:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] [flutter_tools] Add a managed, read-only SDK mode for
 distribution packages

Class: local workaround (distribution packaging). It replaces the
blunter patches Alpine (testing/flutter: no-cache, version, not-in-git)
and the AUR flutter package (no-lock, no-runtime-download, version)
carry for the same purpose.

A distribution installs the SDK read-only (bq builds against a read-only
/usr overlay), with engine artifacts, stamps, the version file and the
flutter_tools snapshot all made at package build time. The stock tool
writes under FLUTTER_ROOT on every run, downloads whatever it finds
stale, and needs a git checkout. It now recognises such an install by
`bin/cache/managed-by`, whose first line names the owner (for example
`pacman (flutter 3.41.9-1)`), and then:

* bin/internal/shared.sh execs the prebuilt snapshot directly: no git
  check, no engine.stamp rewrite, no Dart SDK download, no `pub upgrade`
  and no snapshot rebuild. It also defaults FLUTTER_SUPPRESS_ANALYTICS
  to true (set it to false to opt in), as Alpine and the AUR do.
* Cache.lock() creates no lockfile and checkLockAcquired() passes.
* Cache.updateAll() never updates. If a required artifact set is not up
  to date, it fails with one ToolExit that names every such set and the
  owner, instead of downloading. Artifacts that the command does not
  require are not looked at, so Android/iOS/web pieces need not ship.
* FlutterVersion is read from bin/cache/flutter.version.json, never from
  git, even when tags are to be fetched; a missing or invalid file is an
  error and is not deleted. Framework and engine ages come from the
  dates in that file. The legacy `version` file is not written, and the
  freshness check (git fetch, flutter_version_check.stamp) is skipped.
* `flutter upgrade`, `channel` and `downgrade`, and `precache --force`
  (Cache.clearStampFiles), stop with "Cannot ...: this Flutter SDK is
  managed by <owner> and is read-only."

Nothing changes for an SDK without the marker. Together with the
previous commit, a fully populated managed install is not written to by
the tool at all; PKGBUILD.draft lists the files a package must
pre-generate.

Tests: cache_test (marker and owner; lock and checkLockAcquired;
updateAll fails naming the missing sets, succeeds when complete, ignores
sets not required; clearStampFiles refuses), version_test (file only,
no git, ages from dates; fetchTags keeps the files; no legacy file;
missing or invalid file is an error and is kept), upgrade_test (refuses).
With cache_test, version_test, upgrade, downgrade, precache,
flutter_command_runner and flutter_validator tests: 224 pass.
